        "severity": "minor",
        "evidence": ".md:19-22 sets the SU(2) generators as e_a = -(i/2)τ_a and says they 'correspond to' ½i,½j,½k. The sign/factor convention (−i/2 vs the half-quaternion +½) is asserted without reconciling the −i factor: e_a = −(i/2)τ_a are anti-Hermitian su(2) generators, while ½i,½j,½k are imaginary quaternions — the correspondence is via the iso of step 1 but the sign matching (which τ_a ↔ which quaternion) is left implicit.",
        "notes": "The identification is correct under the step-1 isomorphism (Pauli τ_a map to i·(quaternion units) up to convention), but the precise correspondence τ_1↔i etc. and the −i bookkeeping is not pinned, leaving a reader to reconstruct it. Minor."
      }
